diff --git a/patches/v8/FLYWEB-SECURITY.md b/patches/v8/FLYWEB-SECURITY.md
index 8c67415b..2b916493 100644
--- a/patches/v8/FLYWEB-SECURITY.md
+++ b/patches/v8/FLYWEB-SECURITY.md
@@ -1,3 +1,21 @@
+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 4f37951e9a (crbug 587035145)
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 27-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0014`). V8 15.9 4f37951e9a
+(M159, 15.9.128.45, 27-11; bugs 590972031 and 587035145; cherry-pick of main a5a56b7673). No 15.6 merge yet.
+Adapted to 15.6.75.66: the M159 hunks did not apply because the surrounding code moved (and 15.6 passes `name` to
+`kConstAssign`); the added and removed lines are the same as upstream's. Severity not published.
+
+- Debug-evaluate compiles free identifiers as dynamic lookups. When one resolved to a module import or export,
+  `LoadLookupSlot` returned the cell value without a TDZ check, so reading an uninitialized binding gave the raw
+  `TdzHole` as a value; `StoreLookupSlot` also wrote to bindings that were not initialized yet.
+- Now both throw a `ReferenceError` (`kNotDefined`), as the context-slot path already does. New inspector test
+  `debugger/evaluate-on-call-frame-module-tdz` (its expected output comes from 15.9 and may need a check on 15.6).
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`); no bytecode change.
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): build and run inspector `debugger/evaluate-on-call-frame-module-tdz` and `debugger/*`, and
+mjsunit `modules-*`.
+
